## Context

The conference talk (Econom'IA 2026, 2026-05-27) needs two structural
additions to `slides/slides.tex`:

1. **Take-home message slide** — the single thing the audience should
   remember. Placed near the end, before Q&A. Should synthesise the
   three-experiment arc into one crisp claim.

2. **Methods section (2 slides)** — currently absent or implicit. Audience
   needs to understand the evaluation setup before the results land.
   Two-slide budget:
   - Slide M1: the reference inventory (163 Vietnamese thermal plants),
     the matching protocol (LP fuzzy matcher → F1), and the quality bar
     (4 dimensions: accuracy, coherence, provenance, temporality)
   - Slide M2: experiment design overview — Exp1 (16 models × 5 reps,
     parametric), Exp2 (4 SOTA agents × 2 arms, N=5), Exp3 (pipeline)

Blocked by 0317 because the take-home must be grounded in the final
figures and statistics.

## Take-home message (ratified 2026-05-25)

"Frontier AI agents reach 100-row coverage but fail the provenance bar —
 a tailored pipeline clears it."

Provisional on data analysis — the full wording is contingent on 0313
findings. If the pipeline audit changes the coverage picture or the
provenance result, revisit before implementing.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Author has approved take-home message wording
- [ ] Take-home slide added to `slides.tex`
- [ ] Two Methods slides added (M1: evaluation setup, M2: experiment design)
- [ ] `make slides.pdf` compiles without error
- [ ] Talk fits in allotted time (author to verify live)
